{"title":"2008 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1b Part ii","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1b\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1b</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <i>magic square</i> is a grid of numbers in which the sum of the numbers in each row, in each column, and on each of the two main diagonals is equal to the same number (called the <i>magic constant</i>). \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b_Part_ii&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1b\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b\" title=\"2008 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1b\">Problem 1b</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1b\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A magic square is to be formed using the sixteen integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b_Part_ii&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the magic constant for this magic square and explain how you found it.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b_Part_ii&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> numbers, the magic square would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/6320b3f67b9e4021ebd6feac95c4b5d97004195f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{16} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> rows.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b_Part_i\" title=\"2008 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1b Part i\">part i</a>, the sum of all the numbers in the magic square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3fa029d8ca802c03e5ae47eaf8f71d686cba1be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$136$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. Since each row has the same sum in a magic square and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> rows, the magic constant or sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd096b7252918fcb0ac1fcc478259be80a92ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{136}{4} = \\boxed{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017215445\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 42/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1210/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1238/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   21.048      1 -total\n 65.33%   13.750      1 2008_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n 34.05%    7.166      1 2008_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b\n 28.06%    5.907      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37008:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017215445 and revision id 285965. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}